### User Controller Tests
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiVersion = v1
@userEmail = misty.http@example.com
# Id para las peticiones 3-5. Si las ejecutas de forma individual,
# actualizalo con el "id" devuelto por la peticion 1.
@userId = 1

### 1. Crear usuario
# @name createUser
# Esperado: 201 Created sin campo "password" en la respuesta.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "MistyPassword123",
  "firstName": "Misty",
  "lastName": "Waterflower",
  "phoneNumber": "+5219981234567"
}

### 2. Listar usuarios
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/users
Accept: application/json

> {% client.test("Lista usuarios", function() { client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK"); }); %}

### 3. Obtener usuario creado
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/users/{{userId}}
Accept: application/json

> {% client.test("Obtiene el usuario creado", function() { client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK"); }); %}

### 4. Actualizar usuario creado
# Esperado: 200 OK.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/users/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Misty",
  "lastName": "Waterflower Updated",
  "phoneNumber": "+5219987654321"
}

### 5. Desactivar usuario creado
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/users/{{userId}}

> {% client.test("Desactiva el usuario creado", function() { client.assert(response.status === 204, "Expected 204 No Content"); }); %}

### 6. Rechazar correo duplicado
# Esperado: 409 Conflict (requiere haber ejecutado la peticion 1 antes).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "MistyPassword123",
  "firstName": "Misty",
  "lastName": "Waterflower"
}

### 7. Rechazar datos inválidos
# Esperado: 400 Bad Request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "weak",
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": ""
}

### 8. Usuario inexistente
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/{{apiVersion}}/users/999999
Accept: application/json

> {% client.test("Devuelve 404 para un usuario inexistente", function() { client.assert(response.status === 404, "Expected 404 Not Found"); }); %}
